      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}: I'm sorry. I'm sorry I didn't have time yesterday and wrote a messy sentence.\nI think that the Expression Parameter of the online avatar and the offline avatar should not be synchronized and the value just before the avatar change should be maintained.\nWhether it's the Expression Parameter declared in both avatars or not.\n#Attached video\nWhen I switched from an avatar that implemented costume change to an avatar that did not implement costume change using Expression Parameter, an unexpected value was assigned and the costume was taken off in the video.\nVideo: https://youtu.be/dKsBWmWw2_8",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
